The representation of ECA rules in DNF is well known and has e.g. be studied
by Wolfram [18].
    We however proceed now further by expressing the Boolean operations (∧, ∨, ¬)
arithmetically as
                                  x ∧ y = xy                                           (5)
                                  x ∨ y = x + y − xy
                                    ¬x = 1 − x.
By these operations we attain from the Boolean algebra (A, ∧, ∨, ¬, 1, 0) the
Boolean ring (R, +, −, ·, 1, 0). We found it convenient to express the Boolean
operations as defined above instead of using the usual (mod 2) operations.
    Replacing the Boolean operations in the DNF expressions of ECA rules with
their arithmetic counterparts, we obtain for all ECA algebraic expressions, that
is Boolean polynomials

